பலவே","tr":"palavē","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"பல","tr":"pala"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வே","tr":"vē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"நாட்","parts":[{"text":"நாட்","lemma":"நாட்","gloss":"morning"}],"gloss":"morning","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கள்","parts":[{"text":"கள்","lemma":"கள்","gloss":"toddy"}],"gloss":"toddy"},{"surface":"உண்டு","parts":[{"text":"உண்","lemma":"உண்","gloss":"drink"},{"text":"து","lemma":"து","gloss":"past participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having drunk"},{"surface":"நாள்மகிழ்","parts":[{"text":"நாள்","lemma":"நாள்","gloss":"day/morning"},{"text":"மகிழ்","lemma":"மகிழ்","gloss":"joy"}],"gloss":"morning joy"},{"surface":"மகிழின்","parts":[{"text":"மகிழ்","lemma":"மகிழ்","gloss":"rejoice"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if [one] rejoices"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"யார்க்கும்","parts":[{"text":"யார்","lemma":"யார்","gloss":"who"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"க்கு","gloss":"to"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even/all"}],"gloss":"to anyone"},{"surface":"எளிதே","parts":[{"text":"எளிது","lemma":"எளிது","gloss":"easy thing"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"easy indeed"},{"surface":"தேர்","parts":[{"text":"தேர்","lemma":"தேர்","gloss":"chariot"}],"gloss":"chariot"},{"surface":"ஈதல்லே","parts":[{"text":"ஈதல்","lemma":"ஈதல்","gloss":"giving"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"giving indeed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தொலையா","parts":[{"text":"தொலை","lemma":"தொலை","gloss":"diminish"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"negative relative participle"}],"gloss":"undiminishing"},{"surface":"நல்லிசை","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"நல்","gloss":"good"},{"text":"இசை","lemma":"இசை","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"good fame"},{"surface":"விளங்கு","parts":[{"text":"விளங்கு","lemma":"விளங்கு","gloss":"shine"}],"gloss":"illustrious"},{"surface":"மலயன்","parts":[{"text":"மலயன்","lemma":"மலயன்","gloss":"Malayaṉ"}],"gloss":"Malayaṉ"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மகிழாது","parts":[{"text":"மகிழ்","lemma":"மகிழ்","gloss":"rejoice/be drunk"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ஆது","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without being drunk"},{"surface":"ஈத்த","parts":[{"text":"ஈ","lemma":"ஈ","gloss":"give"},{"text":"த்த","lemma":"த்த","gloss":"past relative participle"}],"gloss":"that was given"},{"surface":"இழையணி","parts":[{"text":"இழை","lemma":"இழை","gloss":"jewels"},{"text":"அணி","lemma":"அணி","gloss":"adorned"}],"gloss":"adorned with jewels"},{"surface":"நெடுந்தேர்","parts":[{"text":"நெடுந்தேர்","lemma":"நெடுந்தேர்","gloss":"tall chariots"}],"gloss":"tall chariots","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பயன்கிழு","parts":[{"text":"பயன்","lemma":"பயன்","gloss":"yield/benefit"},{"text":"கிழு","lemma":"கிழு","gloss":"possessing"}],"gloss":"yielding benefits"},{"surface":"முள்ளூர்","parts":[{"text":"முள்","lemma":"முள்","gloss":"thorn"},{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ஊர்","gloss":"town/hill"}],"gloss":"Muḷḷūr"},{"surface":"மீமிசைப்","parts":[{"text":"மீ","lemma":"மீ","gloss":"high"},{"text":"மிசை","lemma":"மிசை","gloss":"top"},{"text":"ப்","lemma":"ப்","gloss":"sandhi consonant"}],"gloss":"upon the high peak"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பட்ட","parts":[{"text":"பட்ட","lemma":"பட்ட","gloss":"that fell"}],"gloss":"that fell","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மாரி","parts":[{"text":"மாரி","lemma":"மாரி","gloss":"rain"}],"gloss":"rain"},{"surface":"உறையினும்","parts":[{"text":"உறை","lemma":"உறை","gloss":"drop"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"than"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even than the drops"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"are more numerous indeed"}]}],"literal":"Drinking morning toddy, if one rejoices in morning joy, / to anyone easy indeed is giving a chariot! / Malayaṉ of undiminishing good fame and illustriousness, / without being drunk, gave tall chariots adorned with jewels, / which are more numerous than the drops of rain / that fell upon the high peak of fertile Muḷḷūr.","translation":"If one drinks the morning toddy and rejoices in the morning's high spirits, it is easy for anyone to give away a chariot. But Malayaṉ of undiminishing, illustrious fame gave away tall chariots adorned with fine jewels without even being drunk. They are more numerous than the drops of rain that fall upon the high peak of his fertile hill, Muḷḷūr.","modern":"காலையில் வடித்த கள்ளைக் குடித்துவிட்டு, அந்த மகிழ்ச்சியில் திளைத்திருக்கும்போது யாருக்கும் தேரைக் கொடையாகக் கொடுப்பது எளிதானதுதான். ஆனால், அழியாத நல்ல புகழுடன் விளங்கும் மலையமான், தான் மதுவருந்தி மகிழாத நிலையிலும், அணிகலன்கள் பூட்டிய நெடிய தேர்களைக் கொடையாக வழங்கினான். அவனுடைய வளமிக்க முள்ளூர் மலையின் உச்சியில் பெய்த மழையின் துளிகளை விடவும் அவன் கொடையாகக் கொடுத்த தேர்களின் எண்ணிக்கை மிகப்பலவாகும்.","explanation":"In this poem, the poet Kapilar praises the extraordinary generosity of the chieftain Malaiyamāṉ Tirumuṭikkāri. He contrasts ordinary kings with Kāri, noting that while others might easily give away chariots when they are happy and intoxicated on morning toddy, Kāri gives them away in a completely sober state. The chariots he donates are adorned with fine ornaments and are given in immense numbers. To emphasize this boundless charity, the poet uses a hyperbole, comparing the number of chariots given to the countless raindrops falling on Kāri's fertile hill, Muḷḷūr. This poem belongs to the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai as it extols the heroic generosity and noble character of a patron.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}